perator (e.g. `!=`, `[ ... ] && echo PASS`) appears in the proving command — taxonomy item 6 (prose-vs-structured assertion target without an anchored assertion)."],"finding":"AC5's proving command (`jq -r .runner`) emits the runner string but the plan says only 'recording the value on this ticket' — there is no assertion operator that produces a binary PASS/FAIL signal. A reviewer reading the ticket cannot distinguish a genuinely-fixed ticket (runner='llm') from one where someone forgot to re-run the command or recorded a value of 'reused'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f91a7f2c0ff92f74a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC5: 'End to end: on a scratch ticket certified as a bug ...'","norm_id":"n80934cf88605b62a","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An agent runs the command, sees runner='reused' (bug still present), records the string, and marks the AC satisfied — because the criterion says 'record the value', not 'assert it is not reused'.","A later reader cannot tell whether the recorded value was 'llm', 'runner', or 'reused'."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Replace 'recording the value on this ticket' with a shell one-liner that exits non-zero on failure:\n```\nRUNNER=$(rebar review-plan <id> --output json | jq -r .runner)\n[ \"$RUNNER\" != 'reused' ] && echo \"PASS (runner=$RUNNER)\" || (echo \"FAIL (runner=$RUNNER)\" && exit 1)\n```\nThis makes the criterion binary and self-documenting.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an explicit back-out plan to the Approach or Scope section (e.g. 'Revert by removing the two added type-comparison conditionals in reuse.py; no schema change means rollback is immediate and safe') so an operator can act quickly if the change triggers unexpected behavior.","cohort":["COH","E1","T4"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Both reuse paths … never compare type' → the plan changes this behavior for all callers","'Rejected — clear the attestation in the edit command … The reuse functions are the chokepoint every caller flows through' — confirms broad impact","No section of the plan describes how to revert or limit blast radius if the change causes problems","T4 rubric: 'The remedy for a destructive/breaking change is an explicit ROLLBACK / back-out plan or expand-contract — acknowledgement alone is insufficient'"],"finding":"The plan changes observable reuse behavior in two existing functions (idempotent_reuse, verdict_reuse) — a change that consumers relying on cached verdicts will experience — but provides no explicit rollback or back-out path if the change triggers unexpected consequences (e.g. a large-scale storm of re-reviews due to an unanticipated edge case). The plan acknowledges and justifies the behavioral change but T4 requires more than acknowledgement: it requires an explicit reversibility mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8e6a81cec7cc658b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section; Scope section ('src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py')","norm_id":"n698a693d498b664d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A deployment reveals an unexpected edge case (e.g. empty-string type stored as truthy, causing mass re-reviews); without a documented back-out path the operator has no guidance for quick recovery."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a one-sentence rollback note under Approach or Scope: 'Back-out: remove the two added `if base_type and current_type and base_type != current_type` guards; no data migration needed, the sidecar schema is unchanged, and all prior reuse behaviour is immediately restored.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"n